## 7. Demo Configuration

### 7.1 Demo Setup
> After successful compilation, you MUST ask the user for test data to configure the demo page:
> 
> **⚠️ CRITICAL**: This step is MANDATORY and must ALWAYS be completed. Do NOT skip asking for demo configuration.
> 
> **Ask the user for test data**:
> - "Please provide test data for the [Module] create component demo:"
> - **MANDATORY**: "What baseUri should be used for testing? (This is required for API calls)"
> - "What sample values should be used for the form fields?"
> - "Are there any other configuration values needed for the demo?"
> 
> **⚠️ CRITICAL**: Do NOT set a default baseUri if the user has not provided one. The user must explicitly provide the baseUri or edit the demo file later.
> 
> **Update the demo page** (`demo/[module]/create.html`):
> 1. **Open the demo HTML file** in the core library
> 2. **Update the configuration section** with the provided test data:
>    - Set the `BASE_URI` variable to the provided baseUri
>    - Set sample values for form fields
>    - Update any other configuration values as needed
> 3. **Verify the demo works** with the provided test data
> 4. **Test the component** in the browser to ensure it loads correctly
> 
> **Example demo configuration**:
> ```javascript
> // Update these values with the provided test data
> const BASE_URI = "https://your-test-server.com";
> const SAMPLE_NAME = "Sample Library";
> const SAMPLE_DESCRIPTION = "This is a sample library for testing";
