- **Use cmd /c wrapper** for uu5Generate commands, never use PowerShell directly
- **Implement comprehensive validation** at both field and form level
- **Use proper LSI structure** with component uu5Tag as keys
- **Handle nested objects** with dot notation and proper data transformation
- **Test thoroughly** before considering implementation complete
- **Format and compile** code after each major change
- **Configure demo pages** with real test data for demonstration

## 9. Troubleshooting

| Issue | Cause | Solution |
|-------|-------|----------|
| uu5Generate prompts for input | Missing parameters | Always include ALL parameters (--sub-app, --brick-uu5-tag, etc.) |
| PowerShell command fails | Using PowerShell directly | Always use cmd /c wrapper for uu5Generate commands |
| Form validation not working | Missing onValidate prop | Add onValidate prop to Form or individual inputs |
| Modal not closing | Missing cancel/close handlers | Implement proper cancel handler and use close function |
| Form data not matching API | Missing data transformation | Transform form data in handleSubmit to match dtoIn structure |
| LSI labels not displaying | Wrong LSI structure | Use component uu5Tag as main key in LSI file |
| Compilation fails | Syntax errors or missing imports | Fix imports, check syntax, and re-run build |
| Demo page not working | Missing baseUri or test data | Configure demo page with provided test data |